nification X200).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TODENTJ-2-126_F3"/></fig><fig id="F4" position="float"><label>Fig. (4)</label><caption><p>MVD (red arrow) and MCD (green arrow) were significantly increased in oral squamous cell carcinoma. (Original magnification X200).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TODENTJ-2-126_F4"/></fig><fig id="F5" position="float"><label>Fig. (5)</label><caption><p>Mast cell (green arrow) and microvessel (red arrow) revealed with toluidine blue counterstaining (Original magnification X400).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TODENTJ-2-126_F5"/></fig><fig id="F6" position="float"><label>Fig. (6)</label><caption><p>Power curve fit model depicting the correlation between MCD and MVD.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TODENTJ-2-126_F6"/></fig><table-wrap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table 1.</label><caption><p>Correlation of MVD and MCD with Patients&#x02019; Characteristics and Tissue Histopathological Differentiation</p></caption><table frame="border" rules="all" width="100%"><thead><tr><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">Histological Diagnosis</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">Number of Biopsies</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">Microvessel Density (Mean &#x000b1; SD)</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">Mast Cell Density (Mean &#x000b1; SD)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Normal</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">5</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">14.08&#x000b1;6.08</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.32&#x000b1;1.02</td></tr><tr><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Leukoplakia without dysplasia</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">7</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">18.18&#x000b1;2.56</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">4.55&#x000b1;3.26</td></tr><tr><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Leukoplakia with dysplasia</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">12</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">21.79&#x000b1;6.20</t